# Language

Reply to the user in Brazilian Portuguese (pt-BR). These instruction files stay in English.

- Chat replies, PR text, and commit descriptions are pt-BR.
- Code identifiers are English: file names, folders, variables, functions, types, route segments, query keys, setup step ids, audit action names, and commit scopes.
- User-visible product copy is pt-BR: labels, empty states, validation messages, and errors a person reads.
- Code comments are pt-BR and explain why. Cite the business-rule code when one exists (`RN-30`).
- Docs under `docs/` are pt-BR. Routes and code identifiers quoted inside them stay English.

The rest of the project patterns live in `AGENTS.md` files. Read the one next to the code you change (`apps/web`, `packages/core`, `packages/db`, `docs`) before editing that area. Keep this file and the Language section of the root `AGENTS.md` the same.
